A||||6||fierosound||Like POWER STEERING!!!||||1||
Z||000000||fierosound||11-26-1999||12:51 PM||||I've noticed many wishing they had power steering.  I accidentally found the next best thing.  MICHELIN ENERGY MXV4 tires.  <P>These are a "low energy" tire, meaning it has low internal rolling resistance built in.  Therefore you use less fuel.  As a side benefit, steering wheel effort is greatly reduced.  (I stopped and checked to make sure they hadn't accidentally inflated the tires to 80PSI or something!!) I'm basically a one-handed driver, and the only times two hands are necessary are when parking.  Even then, less "grunt" is required.<P>The tires are a performance tire 205R60-15 on front, 210R60-15 on rear.  As I live in Canada I got all-season versions.  Great handling, good ride, less road noise.<P>Highly recommeded.  Anyone else riding on these. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gokart||11-26-1999||08:18 PM||||No, but thanks for the reco, jotted them down cause I'll be lookin' for new ones come spring/summer!||||reg||12
Z||000002||fierosound||05-01-2000||10:47 PM||||More info on those Michelin MXV4 tires.  Covers construction features of the tires, and the sizes available (even 16").<P>I do know they have less rolling resistance.  If I don't leave it in gear, or engage the parking brake, the car will start to roll in my garage, even though the floor appears to be perfectly flat. I guess it's not "perfect", but there is no visibly obvious slope.||||reg||1
Z||000003||pollock||05-02-2000||11:13 AM||||I have power steering in any car i drive...<BR>It's in these cannons just south of my elbows, hehe....<P>Pump up with Hans and Frans!!!!!!!!||||reg||6
Z||000004||IiplayaziI||05-02-2000||09:48 PM||||I met Fierosound the other day and I got to test drive his 87 gt around the block and I must say there is a big improvement on the steering.. I CAN DRINK COFFEE WHILE I DRIVE!!. I personally own an 87 gt as well and I'm most surely gonna look into buying these.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Shiner||05-02-2000||10:50 PM||||I agree with Pollock, you guys are wimps!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>This is not a Honda Accord.  This is a Fiero GT.  To me, a lot of it's appeal is the visceral quality of it.  You have to muscle the damn thing around, and I feel more of a "man and machine" bond with the car.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||batboy||05-02-2000||11:22 PM||||I know nothing about these tires, but I bet they are a fairly hard rubber compound, probably with a high mileage warranty (60K or 75K maybe?). If so, the folks into cornering and performance driving probably won't care for them, but I bet they do increase gas mileage.||||reg||1
